<title>AUSTRIA: Boehler-Uddeholm net down, dividend up.</title>
<headline>Boehler-Uddeholm net down, dividend up.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>High-grade steel maker Boehler-Uddeholm on Tuesday reported the following 1996 earnings details (in billions of schillings unless otherwise indicated):</p>
<p>				  1997	  1996</p>
<p> group sales		17.086	 18.272</p>
<p> group pretax profit     1.35	   1.351</p>
<p> group net profit	  1.00	   1.111</p>
<p> dividend (ATS)		26		25</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full company name is Boehler-Uddeholm AG. The company said it was cautious on the outlook for 1997 and expected slower earnings growth in the first half amid sluggish market conditions in the high-grade steel market.</p>
<p>It added new orders in the first two months of the current year were an average of five percent above last year's.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 53112 274</p>
</text>
